Original commit body from 7e61f9d35de7641808cd694cca09f1af894d4a61:

Addresses WI-zilar. A run that crashed after os.makedirs left
out/cohort-NNN/iter-NNN/<repo>/ present and empty, with the code hash
already recorded. Every later `bakeoff-deep run` then exited 0 printing
"Skipping: hypergumbo code unchanged ... Previous results: <dir>" over a
directory with zero files.

The item's premise that the batch path already had the right check was
wrong. Its guard, `os.listdir(cohort dir)`, is satisfied by the empty
iter-001/, so `run --all` skipped a crashed cohort forever.
bakeoff-broad's batch guard and both scripts' resume "completed" counters
had the same spelling.

All four checks now use _holds_output_files (a file anywhere below). The
single-cohort path says the previous iteration holds no files and runs a
new iteration; the empty directory is kept, since it records the crash.
Tests: a crash is simulated through cmd_run, then single and batch re-runs,
with a control that a real result is still skipped; the predicate is tested
in both scripts, plus a check that no bare listdir truth test remains.

